{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2145 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "3c2396f288e09d7d07a8714333b18784eac952ad45f35a1b88fb1bc91318a1f6" :edb/db-before-t 2144 :edb/db-after-t 2145 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535457 50 #inst "2026-10-09T00:30:39.702Z" 13194139535457 true] [17592186059679 1020 #edb/ref 17592186350234 13194139535457 true] [17592186059681 1020 #edb/ref 17592186350241 13194139535457 true] [17592186059681 1020 #edb/ref 17592186350248 13194139535457 true] [17592186350234 1017 #edb/ref 17592186350235 13194139535457 true] [17592186350234 1089 "q-103533" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350234 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535457 true] [17592186350234 1100 "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\ngiven that $det(A)=4.$" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350234 1113 #uuid "852dcdfe-ad8b-55fc-ab02-b3cb773c55c0" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350234 1145 "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350235 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350236 13194139535457 true] [17592186350235 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350237 13194139535457 true] [17592186350235 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350238 13194139535457 true] [17592186350235 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350239 13194139535457 true] [17592186350235 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350240 13194139535457 true] [17592186350235 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535457 true] [17592186350235 1041 "selection" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350235 1104 #edb/ref 17592186350239 13194139535457 true] [17592186350235 1110 #uuid "3088c17f-4733-53b9-ab9d-7bb976aa64c0" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350236 1034 "4[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350236 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535457 true] [17592186350236 1111 #uuid "6d0b4dc5-34b5-5f8d-a240-32f407402e48" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350237 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350237 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535457 true] [17592186350237 1111 #uuid "1c004200-c624-5ed8-afc6-04b2522df8f0" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350238 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350238 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535457 true] [17592186350238 1111 #uuid "9b15630c-0939-5999-9d68-ae09bdd16144" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350239 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350239 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535457 true] [17592186350239 1111 #uuid "d620ffac-9077-5a93-8b15-d2838786a131" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350240 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350240 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535457 true] [17592186350240 1111 #uuid "ba465286-cacf-5d3a-9dbd-d03815a6a7f8" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350241 1017 #edb/ref 17592186350242 13194139535457 true] [17592186350241 1089 "q-18287" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350241 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535457 true] [17592186350241 1100 "Determine the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A$ $=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]$ if its determinant is $24.$" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350241 1113 #uuid "9b521d3e-8961-5736-a1f0-287985c900e7" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350241 1145 "Since we want the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{31}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{31} & =(-1)^{3+1}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =24-0 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{13}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{31}=\\frac{1}{24}\\cdot 24=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350242 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350243 13194139535457 true] [17592186350242 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350244 13194139535457 true] [17592186350242 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350245 13194139535457 true] [17592186350242 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350246 13194139535457 true] [17592186350242 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350247 13194139535457 true] [17592186350242 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535457 true] [17592186350242 1041 "selection" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350242 1104 #edb/ref 17592186350245 13194139535457 true] [17592186350242 1110 #uuid "f422f321-aec1-5295-860e-00912f1578f3" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350243 1034 "-\\frac{1}{12}" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350243 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535457 true] [17592186350243 1111 #uuid "9fbb3d41-56e7-5eae-90a8-573f9ed56c42" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350244 1034 "\\frac{1}{12}" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350244 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535457 true] [17592186350244 1111 #uuid "8150fcc4-dff1-5d98-81d5-08e1d4c2a98b" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350245 1034 "1" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350245 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535457 true] [17592186350245 1111 #uuid "dbcd3a52-d7d9-5dc0-aa01-6c25c171c46f" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350246 1034 "-1" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350246 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535457 true] [17592186350246 1111 #uuid "3a13a970-f1ca-5977-9640-6b2ef1d621d1" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350247 1034 "-\\frac{1}{24}" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350247 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535457 true] [17592186350247 1111 #uuid "f1100339-16cb-5378-b2f7-e2c7a8b3f367" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350248 1017 #edb/ref 17592186350249 13194139535457 true] [17592186350248 1089 "q-319546" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350248 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535457 true] [17592186350248 1100 "Determine the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nif its determinant is $17.$\n\n${a}_{13}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350248 1113 #uuid "6721d39e-b612-5be9-97a4-8835ad206e75" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350248 1145 "Since we want the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{31}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{31} & =(-1)^{3+1}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\,1\\cdot (1\\cdot 4-0\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{13}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}\\,{c}_{31} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{17}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{17}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350249 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350250 13194139535457 true] [17592186350249 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535457 true] [17592186350249 1041 "field-1" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350249 1104 #edb/ref 17592186350250 13194139535457 true] [17592186350249 1110 #uuid "45cb5e56-e7f3-5703-b61e-344ab9484e6c" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350250 1034 "\\frac{4}{17}" 13194139535457 true] [17592186350250 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535457 true] [17592186350250 1111 #uuid "aaf02b36-d0d0-5f73-80e4-310c5dc697f7" 13194139535457 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-103533" 17592186350234 "q-103533/selection" 17592186350235 "q-103533/selection/11e0fffefaf0c19585beb3fe5d6b182263a904ae2b78fb5b68bfffc3735bf010" 17592186350236 "q-103533/selection/2d01cb1c612bb09c05ff1f4fdc22d33da4c55a3659470b467c8080cb45489dc5" 17592186350237 "q-103533/selection/5037704f2c42ed008396775e0491d66bc8fb38736b50ad4d8ed31371ac381d8a" 17592186350238 "q-103533/selection/8978b159bc14051f9661208f2c7b4572967ea963b05f60d0417a3f594ef1cc15" 17592186350239 "q-103533/selection/b2c82d32d86fb8e2773abed2ce0f95aacb3a6ea0ddb9d33b7708ce63f3f48f82" 17592186350240 "q-18287" 17592186350241 "q-18287/selection" 17592186350242 "q-18287/selection/29f1bd004b0e742e8153de2e3a77945bac059aed56c8ead2bc0011a45597d328" 17592186350243 "q-18287/selection/a7643e7c9a6f47b7e23102a9f593aee2dc956fa29938bf5d470303f0587bc3b1" 17592186350244 "q-18287/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" 17592186350245 "q-18287/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" 17592186350246 "q-18287/selection/f130bed8d6b969dc9fba227edf2